{"id":"10-thresholds","number":10,"slug":"confidence-thresholds","title":"Confidence and thresholds","short":"Thresholds","module":"Probabilities you can act on","summary":"The answer tells you what; the probability tells you whether to act. Here is the three-path pattern (act, confirm, escalate), why thresholds should differ by action, a one-line formula that turns the cost of mistakes into a threshold, and the one thing thresholds cannot protect you from.","voice":"Jessica","scenes":[{"template":"title","chapter":"Intro","narration":"A probability on its own doesn't do anything. Your code turns it into behavior with thresholds. This lesson is about where to put them, and why.","params":{"kicker":"Lesson 10","module":"Module 3 · Probabilities you can act on","title":"Confidence and *thresholds*","subtitle":"The answer says what. The probability says whether to act.","cast":["curly","snap"]},"start":0.5,"dur":10.917,"words":[{"text":"A","s":0.8,"e":0.88},{"text":"probability","s":0.96,"e":1.6},{"text":"on","s":1.68,"e":1.76},{"text":"its","s":1.88,"e":2},{"text":"own","s":2.08,"e":2.48},{"text":"doesn't","s":2.64,"e":2.96},{"text":"do","s":3.04,"e":3.2},{"text":"anything.","s":3.48,"e":4},{"text":"Your","s":4.24,"e":4.4},{"text":"code","s":4.48,"e":4.8},{"text":"turns","s":4.92,"e":5.08},{"text":"it","s":5.12,"e":5.16},{"text":"into","s":5.2,"e":5.36},{"text":"behavior","s":5.44,"e":6.08},{"text":"with","s":6.16,"e":6.32},{"text":"thresholds.","s":6.4,"e":7.12},{"text":"This","s":7.6,"e":7.76},{"text":"lesson","s":7.96,"e":8.16},{"text":"is","s":8.24,"e":8.32},{"text":"about","s":8.4,"e":8.64},{"text":"where","s":8.72,"e":8.88},{"text":"to","s":8.96,"e":9.04},{"text":"put","s":9.12,"e":9.2},{"text":"them,","s":9.28,"e":9.68},{"text":"and","s":9.76,"e":9.84},{"text":"why.","s":9.92,"e":10.56}]},{"template":"statement","chapter":"A second axis","narration":"Here's the idea in one line, from the TypeSafe docs. Use confidence as a second axis. The answer tells you what.